WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.375
This is Coding Exercise 1 for Assignment 4 The goal
is to

00:00:04.388 --> 00:00:09.250
demonstrate that you understand the three different
COUNT patterns Your query should

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:14.438
return three measures from admissions First count
all admission rows using COUNT

00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:20.200
star Second count completed admissions using COUNT
discharge_time because

00:00:20.225 --> 00:00:23.488
a recorded discharge time is the value we are using
to represent

00:00:23.512 --> 00:00:30.125
completion in this exercise Third count unique
patients using COUNT DISTINCT subject_id

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.800
Give each measure a clear alias so the output is
easy to

00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:38.288
interpret Before running the query say what you
expect each number to

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.238
mean The total admissions count may be larger than
the number of

00:00:42.262 --> 00:00:45.862
completed admissions and the number of unique
patients may be smaller than

00:00:45.888 --> 00:00:49.600
the total number of admissions because one patient
can have multiple records

00:00:50.462 --> 00:00:53.912
Click Run and Check then inspect the numbers rather
than relying only

00:00:53.938 --> 00:00:59.000
on the automatic checker If the values are
unexpectedly identical review which

00:00:59.012 --> 00:01:03.212
expression you used in each COUNT The purpose of the
exercise is

00:01:03.225 --> 00:01:05.988
to connect syntax with the population being counted
